---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ImageToolGrid from '../components/ImageToolGrid.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Free Online Image Tools — Resize, Blur, Remove Objects & More | ConvertAnyFile" description="Free browser-based image tools with no source-image upload. Resize, compress, crop, rotate, blur whole images or selected regions, manage transparency, inspect metadata, bulk rename, remove objects, and remove visible watermarks locally.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="site-container hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Image Tools</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Free Online Image Tools</span><h1>Private image tools that run in your browser.</h1><p>Resize, compress, crop, rotate, manage transparent backgrounds, blur whole images or selected areas, inspect metadata, bulk rename files, remove selected objects, or use focused watermark-removal workflows. Working tools keep source-image processing in the browser instead of sending files to a remote conversion queue.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Utility platform preview</span><h2>Everyday transforms and focused interactive edits now share one browser-first hub.</h2><p><a href="/resize-image/"><strong>Resize</strong></a>, <a href="/compress-image/"><strong>Compress</strong></a>, <a href="/crop-image/"><strong>Crop</strong></a>, <a href="/rotate-image/"><strong>Rotate / Flip</strong></a>, <a href="/image-background/"><strong>Image Background</strong></a>, and whole-image <a href="/blur-image/"><strong>Blur</strong></a> use the shared ImageMagick WebAssembly pipeline. P5 adds selected-region blur with a guarded local pixel worker and <a href="/remove-object/"><strong>Remove Object</strong></a> with the shared movable-mask repair editor. <a href="/image-metadata/"><strong>Image Metadata</strong></a> adds local inspection and cleaning, while <a href="/bulk-rename-images/"><strong>Bulk Rename</strong></a> changes filenames without re-encoding image bytes.</p></div><ImageToolGrid /></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Shared behavior where it helps</span><h2>Batch transforms stay fast; interactive edits stay precise.</h2><p>Resize, Compress, Crop, Rotate / Flip, Image Background and whole-image Blur share admission limits, duplicate detection, cancel/retry behavior, per-file downloads and ZIP packaging. Selected-region Blur intentionally uses one image at a time for precise placement. Remove Object uses shared or individual masks when a batch benefits from repeated placement.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Local by design</strong><p>Supported transforms and repairs run on this device. Bulk Rename does not transform pixels at all. Metadata viewing stays local; metadata cleaning creates a newly encoded copy and says so explicitly.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Choose the right tool</span><h2>Start with the change you actually need.</h2></div><div class="comparison-table-wrap"><table class="comparison-table"><thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Best when</th><th>Main controls</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td><a href="/resize-image/"><strong>Resize Image</strong></a></td><td>You need smaller, larger, proportional, or exact image dimensions.</td><td>Target box, exact size, percentage, presets</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/compress-image/"><strong>Compress Image</strong></a></td><td>You need a smaller file while balancing visual quality.</td><td>Quality, Same/JPG/WebP/PNG, size comparison</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/crop-image/"><strong>Crop Image</strong></a></td><td>You need a social, landscape, portrait, exact, or visually positioned batch crop.</td><td>Ratios, exact size, draggable position, nine anchors</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/rotate-image/"><strong>Rotate / Flip</strong></a></td><td>A batch shares an orientation or mirroring problem.</td><td>90/180/270°, horizontal flip, vertical flip</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/image-background/"><strong>Image Background</strong></a></td><td>You already have transparent pixels and need a solid fill or transparency-preserving output.</td><td>Fill/preserve, custom color, PNG/WebP/JPG</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/blur-image/"><strong>Blur Image</strong></a></td><td>You need either one blur strength across a batch or an interactive privacy blur over one selected detail.</td><td>Whole/selected tabs, Rectangle/Ellipse, strength, output</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/remove-object/"><strong>Remove Object</strong></a></td><td>You want to reconstruct a manually selected unwanted object using nearby pixels.</td><td>Shape masks, move/resize/rotate, shared/individual batch</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/image-metadata/"><strong>Image Metadata</strong></a></td><td>You want to inspect detected profiles/attributes or make a cleaned copy.</td><td>Metadata viewer, preserve color profile, cleaner</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/bulk-rename-images/"><strong>Bulk Rename Images</strong></a></td><td>You want consistent filenames without changing image bytes.</td><td>{'{name}'}, {'{n}'}, padding, lowercase</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/gemini-ai-logo-remover/"><strong>Gemini Watermark Remover</strong></a></td><td>A small visible Gemini-style sparkle watermark or similar compact corner mark.</td><td>Circle, 4-Point Star</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="/remove-watermark/"><strong>Remove Watermark</strong></a></td><td>The visible mark can be rectangular, round, diamond-shaped, sparkle-shaped or text.</td><td>Rectangle, Circle, Square, Diamond, Star, Text</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Roadmap discipline</span><h2>Automatic subject isolation still stays separate.</h2><p>P5 intentionally stops before automatic Remove Background. Image Background only fills or preserves transparency that already exists; Remove Object repairs manually selected pixels; neither tool claims automatic subject segmentation.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Smallest processing path</strong><p>Deterministic transforms use the image worker, selected-region blur uses a focused RGBA worker, stateful visual repair uses the mask editor, and filename-only operations skip image re-encoding. Each workflow gets only the processing machinery it needs.</p></div></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
